    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented customerCode de-duplication so that when a computed code collides with an existing owner's code, `-<n>` is appended with the smallest `n \u2265 2` that makes it unique.\n\nThe logic was placed where each piece belongs:\n\n1. **`CustomerCodeGenerator.generateUnique(...)`** \u2014 The generator owns the customerCode *format*, so the suffix-appending logic lives here. It derives the base code via the existing `generate(...)` (reused, not copied) and appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 until a candidate isn't taken. Store access is kept out of this class by taking a `Predicate<String> isTaken`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRepository.existsByCustomerCode(String)`** \u2014 A new query method, implemented in all three repository flavors following the existing `countBy...` patterns:\n   - `SpringDataOwnerRepository` \u2014 Spring Data derived query.\n   - `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl` \u2014 JPQL count.\n   - `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl` \u2014 SQL count on `customer_code`.\n\n3. **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner(...)`** \u2014 Now calls `generateUnique(..., ownerRepository::existsByCustomerCode)`, wiring the store-existence check into the generator. The service keeps its orchestration role without absorbing formatting logic.\n\nThe de-duplicated `customerCode` is stored on the owner (and thus returned), and the test suite is green.",
